{'op': 'retire_proposed_not_applied', 'case': 'C154761', 'why': 'Its whole basis left the PRD: it tests a "Deactivate"/"Activate" text control at the left end of the part dialog footer, from the 9 Sep IN-REVIEW draft. The current PRD (v29, 14 Oct 2026 copy) puts "Delete Part" at the footer\'s left (S13-R6) and sets the status with Part Status and Save (S13-R20 to S13-R22); that path is covered by Story 13\'s cases. Re-checked against v29 on 14 Oct 2026: still no basis.'}
{'op': 'retire_proposed_not_applied', 'case': 'C425639', 'why': 'Rests only on S5-R14 (the dashboard\'s Critical Reorder list leaves out untracked parts), which the PRD as edited 9 Oct 2026 removed. Product\'s answer of 9 Oct 2026, question 13 (Chris Ward): "It will be gone. Dashboard v1 ships first and has no Critical Reorder list. Drop those tests; S5-R14 and S9-E12 are removed from the PRD." Nothing else in the PRD describes a Critical Reorder list, so the case has no source left.'}
{'op': 'retire_proposed_not_applied', 'case': 'C425659', 'why': 'Rests on the dashboard\'s inventory figure (PRD §2 Accounting, v27 bullet "The dashboard\'s inventory figure and the opening inventory used for accounting keep untracked parts, because that stock still sits in the books."), which PRD v29 removed. Product\'s answer of 13 Oct 2026, question 7 (Chris Ward): "No. Dashboard v1 has no inventory figure, and the dashboard references are removed from S9-E11 and from the Accounting section." v29 no longer mentions the dashboard at all. The bullet left in v29 ("The opening inventory used for accounting keeps untracked parts, because that stock still sits in the books.") has no screen a tester can read, and the case\'s Inventory Value check repeats C425630.'}
{'op': 'retire_proposed_not_applied', 'case': 'C425759', 'why': 'Its only basis was S9-E12 (the dashboard\'s Critical Reorder list leaves out inactive parts), which PRD v27 (9 Oct 2026) removed. Product\'s 9 Oct answer, question 13 (Chris Ward): "It will be gone. Dashboard v1 ships first and has no Critical Reorder list. Drop those tests; S5-R14 and S9-E12 are removed from the PRD."'}
{'op': 'retire_proposed_not_applied', 'case': 'C425758', 'why': 'Its only basis was the dashboard\'s inventory figure in S9-E11 and the PRD §2 Accounting bullet. PRD v29 (14 Oct 2026 copy) removed both: S9-E11 now names only Inventory Value and Parts Velocity, and the PRD no longer mentions the dashboard. Product\'s answer of 13 Oct (Chris Ward, question 7): "No. Dashboard v1 has no inventory figure, and the dashboard references are removed from S9-E11 and from the Accounting section." S9-E11 stays covered by C154788, C425756 and C425757.'}
